@startuml maintenance_sequence
title OpenCRM — create maintenance record

autonumber
actor "Organization member" as User
boundary "Workspace API" as Api
control "MaintenanceCreateService" as Create
control "MaintenanceAccess" as Access
control "WorkspaceAccessService" as Workspace
control "OrganizationEntitlementReader" as Entitlements
database "Main PostgreSQL" as Db

User -> Api : create maintenance + detail rows
Api -> Create : CreateAsync
Create -> Access : EnsureCanWriteWorkspaceAsync
Access -> Workspace : require membership and permission
Workspace -> Db : organization, member role, permission overrides
Db --> Workspace : active organization and role
Workspace -> Entitlements : resolve workspace features
alt Commercial mode disabled (default)
  Entitlements -> Entitlements : use platform defaults; skip plan lookup
else Commercial mode enabled
  Entitlements -> Db : load active subscription and plan features
  Db --> Entitlements : subscription snapshot
end
Entitlements --> Workspace : allowed features
Workspace --> Access : write access granted
Access --> Create : authorized

Create -> Create : map detail DTOs to MaintenanceDetail rows
Create -> Db : INSERT Maintenance + MaintenanceDetail rows
Db --> Create : saved IDs
Create -> Db : save history and related state
Create --> Api : maintenance ID
Api --> User : created

note over Workspace,Entitlements
  Membership, role, and permission checks remain required in both modes.
  Commercial mode adds plan-based feature and quota checks.
end note

@enduml
